          <Pad Id="DW074v4jV9rOTdRTc8KXUg" Bounds="1801,1497,400,204" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Most node based environments offer methods to create subpatches which abstract certain functionality and avoid duplicated code all over the place. This is also possible in vvvv using so-called Process Nodes. In fact, every node that is in the Node Browser and that we have used so far, is a Process Node in the background and it is open to the user to create as many of these as desired.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Let's assume we patched along and the result is something like this - three red circles, each with random positions and sizes which are computed on the Create operation and saved into pads.&#xD;&#xA;">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
